{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Qx78fegtsuXXBBGXmSsWqZ","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"CoRL 2026 reviewer guidelines review form\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"CoRL 2026 - Instruction for Authors\",\"url\":\"https://www.corl.org/contributions/instruction-for-authors\"},{\"title\":\"CoRL 2026 Conference | OpenReview\",\"url\":\"https://openreview.net/group?id=robot-learning.org%2FCoRL%2F2026%2FConference\"},{\"title\":\"CoRL 2026 - Call for Papers\",\"url\":\"https://www.corl.org/contributions/call-for-papers\"},{\"title\":\"Reviewer Guidelines — CoRL 2023\",\"url\":\"https://www.corl2023.org/reviewer-guidelines\"},{\"title\":\"Robot Learning Foundation\",\"url\":\"https://www.robot-learning.org/\"},{\"title\":\"CoRL 2026\",\"url\":\"https://www.corl.org/\"},{\"title\":\"ICLR 2026 Reviewer Guide\",\"url\":\"https://iclr.cc/Conferences/2026/ReviewerGuide\"},{\"title\":\"CoRL 2024 - Instruction for Reviews\",\"url\":\"https://2024.corl.org/contributions/instruction-for-reviews\"},{\"title\":\"Instructions for Reviewers\",\"url\":\"https://corl2022.org/instructions-for-reviewers/\"},{\"title\":\"CoRL 2025 Conference | OpenReview\",\"url\":\"https://openreview.net/group?id=robot-learning.org%2FCoRL%2F2025%2FConference\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, I found information about CoRL 2026 submission requirements and some reviewer information, but I didn't find a specific \"reviewer guidelines review form\" document for CoRL 2026. Here's what I found:\n\n## CoRL 2026 Key Information:\n\n**Author Reviewer Requirements:**\nAll submissions must include at least one author who agrees to serve as a CoRL reviewer. They are qualified if they have at least one accepted publication at a previous robotics (CoRL/ ICRA/ IROS/ RSS) or learning conference (ICLR/ NeurIPS/ ICML) or equivalent journal.\n\n**Submission Platform:**\nPapers may be submitted through OpenReview, and submissions can be accessed at the OpenReview platform for CoRL 2026.\n\n## Related Information from Previous CoRL Years:\n\nThe search results included reviewer guidelines from CoRL 2023 and 2024, which provide some insight into the review criteria. Review criteria include: Does the paper address a problem in robot learning? Does it apply or improve a learning-based method, or a learned model? Is the method evaluated in simulation, on real robots, or both? Will the CoRL audience be interested in reading this paper?\n\nFor the most current and specific CoRL 2026 reviewer guidelines and review form, I recommend checking the official CoRL 2026 website or the OpenReview submission platform directly, as the detailed reviewer instructions may not yet be publicly available online or may be in a separate document.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d0b8a538-408e-485b-8d42-e69bd1c2f218","uuid":"3402dd8b-a551-4c10-92e6-8623fbe0a15a","timestamp":"2026-05-23T04:35:22.794Z","tool_use_result":{"query":"CoRL 2026 reviewer guidelines review form","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_01SUX6mdfec6ZoAGDeeLNDWS","content":[{"title":"CoRL 2026 - Instruction for Authors","url":"https://www.corl.org/contributions/instruction-for-authors"},{"title":"CoRL 2026 Conference | OpenReview","url":"https://openreview.net/group?id=robot-learning.org%2FCoRL%2F2026%2FConference"},{"title":"CoRL 2026 - Call for Papers","url":"https://www.corl.org/contributions/call-for-papers"},{"title":"Reviewer Guidelines — CoRL 2023","url":"https://www.corl2023.org/reviewer-guidelines"},{"title":"Robot Learning Foundation","url":"https://www.robot-learning.org/"},{"title":"CoRL 2026","url":"https://www.corl.org/"},{"title":"ICLR 2026 Reviewer Guide","url":"https://iclr.cc/Conferences/2026/ReviewerGuide"},{"title":"CoRL 2024 - Instruction for Reviews","url":"https://2024.corl.org/contributions/instruction-for-reviews"},{"title":"Instructions for Reviewers","url":"https://corl2022.org/instructions-for-reviewers/"},{"title":"CoRL 2025 Conference | OpenReview","url":"https://openreview.net/group?id=robot-learning.org%2FCoRL%2F2025%2FConference"}]},"Based on the search results, I found information about CoRL 2026 submission requirements and some reviewer information, but I didn't find a specific \"reviewer guidelines review form\" document for CoRL 2026. Here's what I found:\n\n## CoRL 2026 Key Information:\n\n**Author Reviewer Requirements:**\nAll submissions must include at least one author who agrees to serve as a CoRL reviewer. They are qualified if they have at least one accepted publication at a previous robotics (CoRL/ ICRA/ IROS/ RSS) or learning conference (ICLR/ NeurIPS/ ICML) or equivalent journal.\n\n**Submission Platform:**\nPapers may be submitted through OpenReview, and submissions can be accessed at the OpenReview platform for CoRL 2026.\n\n## Related Information from Previous CoRL Years:\n\nThe search results included reviewer guidelines from CoRL 2023 and 2024, which provide some insight into the review criteria. Review criteria include: Does the paper address a problem in robot learning? Does it apply or improve a learning-based method, or a learned model? Is the method evaluated in simulation, on real robots, or both? Will the CoRL audience be interested in reading this paper?\n\nFor the most current and specific CoRL 2026 reviewer guidelines and review form, I recommend checking the official CoRL 2026 website or the OpenReview submission platform directly, as the detailed reviewer instructions may not yet be publicly available online or may be in a separate document."],"durationSeconds":6.391330559999998}}
