{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01W8tuwtL8QdN6EYfJLjCWYz","type":"tool_result","content":"# CoRL 2023 Reviewer Guidelines Summary\n\n## Review Dimensions/Criteria\n\nThe guidelines specify six evaluation dimensions:\n\n1. **Originality**: \"Are the problems or methods new?\" Assess novelty, whether it's a valuable combination of existing techniques, and clarity of differentiation from prior work.\n\n2. **Quality**: Evaluate technical soundness, whether claims are supported by theory or experiments, appropriateness of methods, completeness, and author honesty about strengths/weaknesses.\n\n3. **Clarity**: Judge writing quality, organization, and whether experts could reproduce results from the information provided.\n\n4. **Significance**: Determine if results matter and whether the work advances the field demonstrably or offers unique approaches.\n\n5. **Relevance**: Assess whether the paper addresses robot learning problems, uses learning-based methods, and will interest the CoRL audience.\n\n6. **Limitations**: Appreciate honestly-reported limitations while identifying unreported flaws that significantly impact the work's validity.\n\n## Scoring Scale\n\n**The document does not specify a numerical scoring scale** for reviews. It references review forms and scoring but doesn't define what each score means.\n\n## Key Evaluation Principles\n\nReviewers should avoid common mistakes like rejecting work without citing prior work, dismissing papers for lacking datasets/code, or assuming state-of-the-art performance alone determines acceptance quality."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d0b8a538-408e-485b-8d42-e69bd1c2f218","uuid":"adc14a0a-ce52-4e22-958b-349f932c4fb1","timestamp":"2026-05-23T04:35:46.395Z","tool_use_result":{"bytes":105095,"code":200,"codeText":"OK","result":"# CoRL 2023 Reviewer Guidelines Summary\n\n## Review Dimensions/Criteria\n\nThe guidelines specify six evaluation dimensions:\n\n1. **Originality**: \"Are the problems or methods new?\" Assess novelty, whether it's a valuable combination of existing techniques, and clarity of differentiation from prior work.\n\n2. **Quality**: Evaluate technical soundness, whether claims are supported by theory or experiments, appropriateness of methods, completeness, and author honesty about strengths/weaknesses.\n\n3. **Clarity**: Judge writing quality, organization, and whether experts could reproduce results from the information provided.\n\n4. **Significance**: Determine if results matter and whether the work advances the field demonstrably or offers unique approaches.\n\n5. **Relevance**: Assess whether the paper addresses robot learning problems, uses learning-based methods, and will interest the CoRL audience.\n\n6. **Limitations**: Appreciate honestly-reported limitations while identifying unreported flaws that significantly impact the work's validity.\n\n## Scoring Scale\n\n**The document does not specify a numerical scoring scale** for reviews. It references review forms and scoring but doesn't define what each score means.\n\n## Key Evaluation Principles\n\nReviewers should avoid common mistakes like rejecting work without citing prior work, dismissing papers for lacking datasets/code, or assuming state-of-the-art performance alone determines acceptance quality.","durationMs":5153,"url":"https://www.corl2023.org/reviewer-guidelines"}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01BH7RKzd35wGsySWVZwBBZ1","type":"tool_result","content":"# CoRL 2024 Reviewer Guidelines\n\nBased on the provided page content, here's what is specified:\n\n## Review Criteria\nPapers are evaluated on:\n- **Significance and novelty** of theoretical or empirical results\n- **Objectivity** of established results and potential for scientific/technological impact\n- **Relevance to robotic learning**\n\nThe guidelines note: \"Papers with both experimental and theoretical results relevant to robot learning are welcome.\"\n\n## Scope Requirements\nSubmissions must demonstrate relevance through either:\n- **Intent**: \"Explicitly address a learning question for physical robots\" OR\n- **Outcome**: \"Test the proposed learning solution on physical robots\"\n\n## Notable Gaps\n\nThe document does **not** include:\n- A numerical scoring scale (1-10 or otherwise)\n- Specific review dimensions or scoring rubrics\n- Definitions of what individual scores mean\n- Conference acceptance rate information\n- Detailed evaluation criteria beyond the general principles listed\n\nThe page focuses on desk rejection criteria and reviewer qualifications rather than the complete scoring framework for accepted submissions."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d0b8a538-408e-485b-8d42-e69bd1c2f218","uuid":"e7d99e13-9e2e-4f0e-94dd-a16de4109041","timestamp":"2026-05-23T04:35:48.647Z","tool_use_result":{"bytes":134077,"code":200,"codeText":"OK","result":"# CoRL 2024 Reviewer Guidelines\n\nBased on the provided page content, here's what is specified:\n\n## Review Criteria\nPapers are evaluated on:\n- **Significance and novelty** of theoretical or empirical results\n- **Objectivity** of established results and potential for scientific/technological impact\n- **Relevance to robotic learning**\n\nThe guidelines note: \"Papers with both experimental and theoretical results relevant to robot learning are welcome.\"\n\n## Scope Requirements\nSubmissions must demonstrate relevance through either:\n- **Intent**: \"Explicitly address a learning question for physical robots\" OR\n- **Outcome**: \"Test the proposed learning solution on physical robots\"\n\n## Notable Gaps\n\nThe document does **not** include:\n- A numerical scoring scale (1-10 or otherwise)\n- Specific review dimensions or scoring rubrics\n- Definitions of what individual scores mean\n- Conference acceptance rate information\n- Detailed evaluation criteria beyond the general principles listed\n\nThe page focuses on desk rejection criteria and reviewer qualifications rather than the complete scoring framework for accepted submissions.","durationMs":7502,"url":"https://2024.corl.org/contributions/instruction-for-reviews"}}
