f a rater-blinded, retrospective study\",\"url\":\"https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC1482713/\"},{\"title\":\"What Have We Learned from OpenReview?\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2103.05885\"}]\n\nI've completed the web search for the CoRL 2024/2025 review form information. Based on my search results, I was able to find a reference to the CoRL 2024 instructions for reviews page (at 2024.corl.org), but the search results only show partial content from that page. The full details about the specific scoring scale with categories like \"strong accept,\" \"accept,\" and \"reject\" were not fully captured in the search results.\n\nFrom the search results, I found:\n\n1. CoRL 2024 submissions are evaluated based on the significance and novelty of the results, either theoretical or empirical.\n\n2. The main review part of the review form asks for an evaluation of originality, quality, clarity, significance, relevance and limitations of the work.\n\n3. Papers that receive all reviews in the \"reject\" range in the initial round will not proceed to the rebuttal phase, which indicates that CoRL uses a scoring scale that includes \"reject\" as one category.\n\nHowever, I was unable to locate the complete scoring scale showing the exact categories (such as \"strong accept,\" \"weak accept,\" \"accept,\" \"borderline,\" \"reject,\" \"strong reject,\" etc.) and their numerical values from the OpenReview review form for CoRL 2024 or 2025. The search results returned the main OpenReview pages but not the detailed review form specification. To see the full review form details, you would need to visit the OpenReview pages directly at https://openreview.net/group?id=robot-learning.org/CoRL/2024/Conference or https://openreview.net/group?id=robot-learning.org/CoRL/2025/Conference, or check the detailed instructions at https://2024.corl.org/contributions/instruction-for-reviews.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d0b8a538-408e-485b-8d42-e69bd1c2f218","uuid":"ab319724-9eaf-416f-afb4-12aacd2835e4","timestamp":"2026-05-23T04:36:15.150Z","tool_use_result":{"query":"CoRL 2024 2025 OpenReview review form overall score scale \"strong accept\" \"accept\" \"reject\"","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_018m8MurwbPhQaRVeWyYSnk1","content":[{"title":"CoRL 2024 | OpenReview","url":"https://openreview.net/group?id=robot-learning.org/CoRL/2024"},{"title":"CoRL 2024 Conference | OpenReview","url":"https://openreview.net/group?id=robot-learning.org%2FCoRL%2F2024%2FConference"},{"title":"CoRL 2025 | OpenReview","url":"https://openreview.net/group?id=robot-learning.org/CoRL/2025"},{"title":"CoRL 2025 Conference | OpenReview","url":"https://openreview.net/group?id=robot-learning.org%2FCoRL%2F2025%2FConference"},{"title":"CoRL | OpenReview","url":"https://openreview.net/group?id=robot-learning.org%2FCoRL"},{"title":"Reviewer Guidelines — CoRL 2023","url":"https://www.corl2023.org/reviewer-guidelines"},{"title":"What Drives Paper Acceptance? A Process-Centric Analysis of Modern Peer Review","url":"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2509.25701"},{"title":"Can Small and Reasoning Large Language Models Score Journal Articles for Research Quality and Do Averaging and Few-shot Help?","url":"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2510.22389"}]},"The search results returned general OpenReview pages but didn't provide the specific review form details. Let me search more specifically for the CoRL review form and scoring scale information.",{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_01D5enTQVBvuSjMv2WtcCKGP","content":[{"title":"Reviewer Guidelines","url":"https://neurips.cc/Conferences/2022/ReviewerGuidelines"},{"title":"2025 Reviewer Guidelines","url":"https://neurips.cc/Conferences/2025/ReviewerGuidelines"},{"title":"2024 Reviewer Guidelines","url":"https://neurips.cc/Conferences/2024/ReviewerGuidelines"},{"title":"Uncertainty in Artificial Intelligence","url":"https://www.auai.org/uai2023/review