017, Ye et al. 2021\n- Safety in robotic manipulation: Ames et al. 2019 (CBFs), SafeLIBERO 2025\n- Occupancy prediction: Tong et al. 2023, Wei et al. 2023, Tian et al. 2024\n\n**Key results:**\n| Condition | Seeds | TSR | CAR | Δ CAR |\n|-----------|-------|-----|-----|-------|\n| Vanilla | 3 | 0.907±0.009 | 0.780±0.012 | — |\n| Full OCC | 3 | 0.894±0.050 | 0.797±0.032 | +1.7pp |\n| Random OCC | 3 | 0.869±0.029 | 0.789±0.031 | +0.9pp |\n| Depth | 4 | 0.889±0.042 | 0.780±0.037 | +0.0pp |\n| Cutoff@35K | 3 | 0.902±0.023 | 0.777±0.018 | -0.3pp |\n| Detach OCC | 3 | 0.812±0.163 | 0.746±0.002 | -3.4pp |\n\n**Discussion points:**\n- \"Gradient flow as binary switch\" — any amount ≥30% prevents degradation\n- \"Why does detaching hurt?\" — two hypotheses: (1) dead branch noise, (2) distributional shift without adaptation. Cannot adjudicate between them.\n- \"Spatial content does not matter\" — challenges intuition about 3D spatial supervision improving collision avoidance\n- Practical guidelines: always maintain gradient flow, content choice secondary, partial training suffices\n\n**Limitations acknowledged:** Single benchmark, single VLA architecture, limited mechanism depth, statistical power (n=3).\n\n**Appendix A (CKA):** Modest differences, all CKA >0.85, \"consistent with but does not establish causal link.\"\n**Appendix B (Gradient):** Null result — cosine similarity near zero, Full OCC ≈ Random OCC in gradient statistics.\n\n**Experiment design context (from review_context.yaml):**\nThe narrative guidance notes: \"核心数据（Detach 损害，Glass's Δ ≈ 2.8）稳健但不惊艳。CKA/gradient 分析信号嘈杂，降级为 supplementary exploratory analysis。\" The paper's own assessment is that mechanism depth is shallow — \"no causal mechanism, single benchmark, CKA/gradient null results.\" The paper's self-assessed CoRL fit is \"borderline\" with 30-45% acceptance probability.\n\nKey narrative assessment from context:\n- C1 (Detach harm): 8/10 — hard data, 3-seed consistent, large effect\n- C2 (Factorial study): 5/10 — methodological contribution, limited novelty\n- C3 (Practical guideline): 6/10 — useful but obvious in hindsight\n- Mechanism depth: 3/10 — CKA/gradient null results, no causal explanation\n- Overall CoRL fit: 5/10 — borderline\n\n## Your Task (R2: Novelty + Related Work)\nWrite a full review covering:\n1. **Summary** (2-3 sentences)\n2. **Strengths** (focus on novelty of contributions, positioning within related work, significance of findings)\n3. **Weaknesses** (focus on novelty limitations, missing related work, overclaiming, framing issues)\n4. **Questions for Authors** (specific, actionable)\n5. **Minor Issues**\n6. **Scores**: Overall (1-10), Originality (1-5), Quality (1-5), Clarity (1-5), Significance (1-5), Relevance (1-5), Confidence (1-5)\n\nBe rigorous. Evaluate whether the contributions are novel enough for CoRL, whether related work is comprehensive, and whether the claims are appropriately calibrated to the evidence.\n","uuid":"a1020b67-3af2-4e03-93a8-3f9ec4aa6dad","session_id":"d0b8a538-408e-485b-8d42-e69bd1c2f218"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"You are Reviewer 2 (R2) for a CoRL 2026 submission. Your focus is **Novelty and Related Work**. Produce an independent, blinded review.\n\n## CoRL Review Criteria\nCoRL evaluates on: Originality, Quality, Clarity, Significance, Relevance (to robot learning), Limitations. Acceptance rate ~30-35%. Scale: 1-10 (10=Strong Accept, 8=Accept, 6=Weak Accept, 5=Borderline, 4=Weak Reject, 3=Reject, 1=Strong Reject).\n\n## Paper Summary\n**Title:** \"Does Auxiliary Spatial Supervision Make VLAs Safer? An Empirical Investigation\"\n\nThe paper conducts a factorial study of auxiliary spatial supervision in VLA fine-tuning, varying auxiliary task content (BEV occupancy, egocentric depth, random noise) and gradient flow configuration (full, detached, partial/cutoff). Six conditions, 3-4 seeds each, on SafeLIBERO-Spatial.\n\n**Architecture:** OpenVLA (7.65B params), DINOv2+SigLIP encoders, Llama-2 decoder, LoRA (rank=32, α=16). Auxiliary heads: OccHead (1.2M params, Focal Loss) and DepthHead (Smooth L1). Exponential decay loss weight: w(t) = 0.01·exp(-t/50000).\n\n**Six conditions:** Vanilla (no aux head), Full OCC (BEV occ + grad flow), Random OCC (random + grad flow), Depth (ego depth + grad flow), Cutoff@35K (partial grad flow 70%), Detach OCC (no grad flow).\n\n**Three claims:**\n1. Detaching gradients actively harms safety (CAR -3.4pp, Glass's Δ=2.83, p<0.01)\n2. Spatial content is secondary (Full OCC, Random OCC, Depth all within 1.7pp of Vanilla, no significant differences)\n3. Gradient flow operates as binary switch (Cutoff@35K ≈ Vanilla, Detach significantly worse)\n\n**Related Work coverage:**\n- VLA models: Brohan et al. 2023 (RT-2), Kim et al. 2024 (OpenVLA), Team et al. 2024 (Octo)\n- Auxiliary tasks in robot learning: Jaderberg et al. 2017 (UNREAL), Mirowski et al. 2017, Ye et al. 2021\n- Safety in robotic manipulation: Ames et al. 2019 (CBFs), SafeLIBERO 2025\n- Occupancy prediction: Tong et al. 2023, Wei et al. 2023, Tian et al. 2024\n\n**Key results:**\n| Condition | Seeds | TSR | CAR | Δ CAR |\n|-----------|-------|-----|-----|-------|\n| Vanilla | 3 | 0.907±0.009 | 0.780±0.012 | — |\n| Full OCC | 3 | 0.894±0.050 | 0.797±0.032 | +1.7pp |\n| Random OCC | 3 | 0.869±0.029 | 0.789±0.031 | +0.9pp |\n| Depth | 4 | 0.889±0.042 | 0.780±0.037 | +0.0pp |\n| Cutoff@35K | 3 | 0.902±0.023 | 0.777±0.018 | -0.3pp |\n| Detach OCC | 3 | 0.812±0.163 | 0.746±0.002 | -3.4pp |\n\n**Discussion points:**\n- \"Gradient flow as binary switch\" — any amount ≥30% prevents degradation\n- \"Why does detaching hurt?\" — two hypotheses: (1) dead branch noise, (2) distributional shift without adaptation. Cannot adjudicate between them.\n- \"Spatial content does not matter\" — challenges intuition about 3D spatial supervision improving collision avoidance\n- Practical guidelines: always maintain gradient flow, content choice secondary, partial training suffices\n\n**Limitations acknowledged:** Single benchmark, single VLA architecture, limited mechanism depth, statistical power (n=3).\n\n**Appendix A (CKA):** Modest differences, all CKA >0.85, \"consistent with but does not establish causal link.\"\n**Appendix B (Gradient):** Null result — cosine similarity near zero, Full OCC ≈ Random OCC in gradient statistics.\n\n**Experiment design context (from review_context.yaml):**\nThe narrative guidance notes: \"核心数据（Detach 损害，Glass's Δ ≈ 2.8）稳健但不惊艳。CKA/gradient 分析信号嘈杂，降级为 supplementary exploratory analysis。\" The paper's own assessment is that mechanism depth is shallow — \"no causal mechanism, single benchmark, CKA/gradient null results.\" The paper's self-assessed CoRL fit is \"borderline\" with 30-45% acceptance probability.\n\nKey narrative assessment from context:\n- C1 (Detach harm): 8/10 — hard data, 3-seed consistent, large effect\n- C2 (Factorial study): 5/10 — methodological contribution, limited novelty\n- C3 (Practical guideline): 6/10 — useful but obvious in hindsight\n- Mechanism depth: 3/10 — CKA/gradient null results, no causal explanation\n- Overall CoRL fit: 5/10 — borderline\n\n## Your Task (R2: Novelty + Related Work)\nWrite a full review covering:\n1. **Summary** (2-3 sentences)\n2. **Strengths** (focus on novelty of contributions, positioning within related work, significance of findings)\n3. **Weaknesses** (focus on novelty limitations, missing related work, overclaiming, framing issues)\n4. **Questions for Authors** (specific, actionable)\n5. **Minor Issues**\n6. **Scores**: Overall (1-10), Originality (1-5), Quality (1-5), Clarity (1-5), Significance (1-5), Relevance (1-5), Confidence (1-5)\n\nBe rigorous. Evaluate whether the contributions are novel enough for CoRL, whether related work is comprehensive, and whether the claims are appropriately calibrated to the evidence.\n"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_018fH1bx851t3wjnet2HMt5b","session_id":"d0b8a538-408e-485b-8d42-e69bd1c2f218","uuid":"75e62bf2-536f-4606-8599-80ae5a9a0821","timestamp":"2026-05-23T04:37:36.775Z"}
